ncurrency n=68/53, but the repo has no cited code-v5 calibration artifact and committed code-v3/v4 docs contain different counts. Decision-needed: either (A) provide/commit the code-v5 calibration artifact under docs/experiments and cite it in the routing _comments, then re-review/execute; or (B) defer/return this to the calibration session to produce that artifact before routing changes. Recommendation: B unless the calibration data is immediately available, because landing threshold changes without reproducible evidence would violate ADR 0036/0054 calibration precedent. No code changes made for this ticket; no force used.","timestamp":1788905731231063001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Calibration prerequisite update: Gerrit 2861 is MERGED and ticket precranial-clerical-xiphias (2629-03a8-f93b-4457) is closed. The reproducible artifact now exists at docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration-code-v5.md, so the prior decision-needed blocker is resolved; proceeding to re-review and implement only the threshold-routing scope.","timestamp":1788969157593859001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA/TDD evidence: root cause is routing drift after IMPACT_MODEL_VERSION moved to code-v5 while security/concurrency thresholds still reflected earlier corpora; prerequisite Gerrit 2861 supplied the missing reproducible code-v5 calibration artifact. RED: after updating tests first, targeted suite failed on unchanged routing/docs (5 failures: superseded decision absent; concurrency not in blocking set; security/concurrency old thresholds). GREEN: updated only routing, derived tests, and calibration-doc supersession. Validation: targeted six-file suite passed (74 passed); derived-threshold temporary 0.60 oracle passed (18 passed) and was restored; make lint passed; make typecheck passed; full make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2 passed with GIT_CONFIG_* unset.","timestamp":1788980739437670001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Completion evidence: Gerrit 2934 merged at 033a9a11e741 with LLM-Review+1, Verified+1, unresolved comments 0. CI_RESULT {\"run_id\":\"34393313495\",\"status\":\"passed\",\"fixes_applied\":[\"implemented code-v5 security/concurrency routing thresholds\",\"updated derived routing tests and code-v4 supersession record\"],\"retry_count\":0}. Local verification: RED targeted suite failed on unchanged routing/docs (5 failures); GREEN targeted six-file suite passed (74 passed); temporary security threshold 0.60 derived-test oracle passed (18 passed) and was restored; make lint/typecheck passed; full make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2 passed with GIT_CONFIG_* unset.","timestamp":1788983425520709001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788904867623424001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"703e7f5b-cfed-46c5-ba35-9b9d10220c61","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"2629-03a8-f93b-4457"},{"link_uuid":"44b66c61-e860-498d-99fc-35d8f1ba6ccf","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c6f7-74d9-9c6c-47ee"},{"link_uuid":"1b8cc06a-fea2-4212-a9c7-2d36c9a2c3dd","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b87b-df4d-de9a-4c7d"}],"description":"## Problem\n\nCode-review routing still uses thresholds tuned on pre-code-v5 corpora. ADR 0036 forbids pooling across impact-model versions. Prerequisite `2629-03a8-f93b-4457` has now landed the reproducible code-v5 calibration generator/record in Gerrit 2861, including `docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration-code-v5.md`. This ticket only consumes that record and applies the two approved routing flips.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json`: set `security.block_threshold` to 0.45 while keeping it blocking; set `concurrency` to `default_posture: blocking`, `block_threshold: 0.52`, `blocking_enabled: true`. Both `_comment`s cite `3055-e92d-7063-4a32` and the code-v5 calibration record.\n- `tests/unit/test_code_review_blocking_replay.py`: remove every stale 0.54/0.45 security-threshold literal (docstring, comments, constants) and derive behavioral assertions from `reg.threshold_for([\"security\"])`.\n- `tests/unit/test_code_review_criteria_routing.py`: remove `concurrency` from the advisory-disjoint literal; teach the code-v4 decision-table test about `superseded` rows via an explicit parsed `superseded_by` column; require `flip` and `superseded` decisions.\n- `tests/unit/test_code_review_ws2.py`: add `concurrency` to the deliberate approved blocking set and cite this ticket/code-v5 record near the pin.\n- `tests/unit/test_impact_model_versioning.py`: add `concurrency` to the approved blocking set and update the security threshold pin to 0.45, with this ticket/code-v5 record cited near the pin.\n- `tests/unit/test_code_review_triggers.py`: update direct and overlay-merged concurrency posture pins from 0.95/advisory to 0.52/blocking.\n- `tests/unit/test_code_review_criteria_normalization.py`: update stale prose/assert messages that say security blocks at 0.54; existing priority fixtures already use 0.9 and need no threshold-value assertion change.\n- `docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration.md`: preserve the code-v4 concurrency measurement at `thr` 0.54, but mark its decision `superseded` and point a new `superseded_by` column at `docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration-code-v5.md`. Give every table row a cell in the new column (`—` for non-superseded rows).\n\nNo generator changes are in scope; they landed in prerequisite Gerrit 2861.\n\n## Evidence\n\nThe code-v5 record adjudicates newly-blocking findings in `[proposed, current)`: `security@0.45` has 13/13 TP-blockworthy, 0 nits, 0 FP, and 1.43% change friction; `concurrency@0.52` has 2/2 TP-blockworthy, 0 nits, 0 FP, and 0.29% change friction. The prior concurrency hold was only because code-v4 had n=1 below `MIN_N=25`; code-v5 has n=68 / 53 surviving. The same record rejects a severity-floor alternative due nit/FP load.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nRouting `maintainability`; changing `impact_code` or severity floors; prompt remediations; re-running or editing the calibration generator.\n\n## Back-out\n\nRevert the two JSON entries to their prior values (`security` 0.54; `concurrency` 0.95/advisory/disabled) and restore the dependent test expectations. No migration or feature flag is involved.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] Security threshold is 0.45 and blocking. Oracle: `python -c \"import json;d=json.load(open('src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json'));assert d['security']['block_threshold']==0.45 and d['security']['blocking_enabled'] is True\"`.\n- [x] Concurrency threshold is 0.52 and blocking. Oracle: `python -c \"import json;d=json.load(open('src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json'));c=d['concurrency'];assert c['block_threshold']==0.52 and c['blocking_enabled'] is True and c['default_posture']=='blocking'\"`.\n- [x] Both routing entries cite this ticket. Oracle: `[ \"$(grep -c \"3055-e92d-7063-4a32\" src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json)\" -ge 2 ]`.\n- [x] Both routing entries cite the code-v5 record. Oracle: `[ \"$(grep -c \"code-review-threshold-calibration-code-v5\" src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json)\" -ge 2 ]`.\n- [x] Other criteria keep their posture/thresholds. Oracle: compare `default_posture`, `block_threshold`, and `blocking_enabled` for all non-`security`/`concurrency` entries against `git show HEAD:src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json` in a Python assertion script.\n- [x] Blocking-replay tests derive thresholds and retain nit coverage. Oracle: `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_code_review_blocking_replay.py tests/unit/test_code_review_criteria_routing.py -q`; `[ \"$(grep -Ec \"0\\.(54|45)\" tests/unit/test_code_review_blocking_replay.py)\" -eq 0 ]`; `grep -c \"def test_nit_priority_below_threshold_does_not_block\" tests/unit/test_code_review_blocking_replay.py` returns 1.\n- [x] Derived blocking-replay tests survive a temporary security threshold change to 0.60 without test edits, then the file is restored to 0.45.\n- [x] Blocking-set, impact-version, trigger-posture, and stale-comment pins are updated. Oracle: `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_code_review_ws2.py tests/unit/test_impact_model_versioning.py tests/unit/test_code_review_triggers.py tests/unit/test_code_review_criteria_normalization.py -q`; `grep -R \"security.*0.54\\|0.54.*security\" tests/unit/test_code_review_criteria_normalization.py tests/unit/test_code_review_blocking_replay.py` returns no stale security-threshold prose.\n- [x] Code-v4 replay table still records code-v4 measurement and points to the later record. Oracle: `grep -n \"| concurrency | 0.54 |\" docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration.md` matches; that row decision is `superseded`; its `superseded_by` cell names the code-v5 record.\n- [x] `make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2` is green with documented `GIT_CONFIG_*` variables unset.\n- [x] Gerrit change is MERGED with LLM-Review+1 and Verified+1.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json","reason":"security 0.54->0.45 and concurrency advisory->blocking@0.52; comments cite this ticket and code-v5 calibration record"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_code_review_blocking_replay.py","reason":"derive security threshold behavior from routing instead of stale literals"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_code_review_criteria_routing.py","reason":"accept superseded code-v4 row with explicit later-record pointer and updated blocking advertisement"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_code_review_ws2.py","reason":"update approved blocking-set pin for concurrency"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_impact_model_versioning.py","reason":"update approved blocking-set and security threshold pins"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_code_review_triggers.py","reason":"update concurrency posture and overlay merge pins"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_code_review_criteria_normalization.py","reason":"remove stale security@0.54 prose"},{"path":"docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration.md","reason":"mark code-v4 concurrency row superseded by code-v5 record without changing measured values"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","2629-03a8-f93b-4457"],["relates_to","b87b-df4d-de9a-4c7d"],["relates_to","c6f7-74d9-9c6c-47ee"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"d287241d-277b-4477-a5f1-47599c6ce3dd","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["calibration","code-review"],"ticket_id":"3055-e92d-7063-4a32","ticket_type":"task","title":"Route security at 0.45 and concurrency blocking at 0.52 from the code-v5 calibration","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["1827240f-0578-4d7a-82fa-b015133a0331","c720d3b5-1439-4c93-a6c7-b7d5252e3ce7","27ad8148-5c3a-4123-8259-a028d71c0f88","8d552e83-cd7d-4f0d-84b6-33c99b2699df","6fe7dc14-f98f-4849-b81a-6584553691f9","36b97ef8-558e-43af-9f51-d7233e2c5c4a","d6d51d60-dde4-448a-97ef-af35ffb00544","abd37e14-75a8-46a6-aa1a-1d709d89d1a3","d4c2e10e-5eb4-476e-84a2-d250c2838047","6f66dc7e-53d8-4dec-a5dc-8d7d5234219d","44b66c61-e860-498d-99fc-35d8f1ba6ccf","9a9e131c-1361-4e29-86d1-711af7879811","fa27f5b5-4deb-4d05-b5ae-cb08c2283c86","1b8cc06a-fea2-4212-a9c7-2d36c9a2c3dd","d287241d-277b-4477-a5f1-47599c6ce3dd","da4e50ee-a5ce-4bda-9336-aa01572fe822"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788994514238784001,"uuid":"b783a33c-b4dc-4fdf-b3d5-5eda3e5b4a14"}